' S-179: VAL() returns a Double (VAL("2.75") = 2.75, S-137's own AST fix); native/legacy called an
' INTEGER-returning runtime helper (__uxb_rt_val_i64 / atoi) for it while every caller reads the result
' as F64 -- the raw integer bits then got misread through XMM0 as if they were already a double's bit
' pattern (VAL("40") printed as the denormal 40's bits decode to, ~1.976e-322; VAL("40")+7 printed 7).
DIM n AS F64
n = VAL("40")
PRINT n
PRINT VAL("40") + 7
PRINT VAL("2.75")
PRINT VAL("-3.5") * 2
PRINT VAL("")
PRINT VAL("abc")
